# Research Coach

Web app that guides undergrads through starting a research project in any
field. Core differentiator: the AI never loses project context. Structured
project state in Postgres (Project Brain) is the source of truth; assemble
prompts from it on every call. Do NOT rely on chat history for memory.

# Stack

Next.js 16 App Router, TypeScript (strict), Supabase (auth, Postgres, RLS),
Groq (primary) and Google Gemini (fallback) from server routes only,
OpenAlex for papers. Tailwind v4 + shadcn/ui. See CLAUDE.md for details.

# Hard rules

- API keys only in server code. Never expose them to the client.
- Citations: only papers in the `papers` table or returned by the
  `recommend_readings` tool (real OpenAlex results). Never invent references.
- The AI teaches and critiques; it does not ghostwrite the paper, question,
  or novelty claim.
- Research-progress changes are PROPOSED as patches the user accepts or
  rejects. Only profile fields (interest, background, experience level,
  constraints) may be written directly by the coach (`update_profile`).
- Prompt assembly is a pure function in `lib/prompt/assemble.ts` with tests.
- All tables use RLS scoped to `auth.uid()`.
- Validate API inputs with zod. Validate model tool output before saving.
- Small, reviewable commits. Explain what changed after each task.

# Scope

Phase 1 (Orient) and Phase 2 (Find your question) only.
Do not build experiment or paper-writing features.
